  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nWhat is Comet Halley's orbital period in months? Comet Halley orbits the sun every 76 years. Comet Halley's appearances are treated as occurring exactly once every 75 years. One year is defined as 12 months.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Comet Halley’s orbital period is given as \\(76\\) years. Since \\(1\\) year equals \\(12\\) months:\n\n\\[\n76 \\times 12 = 912\n\\]\n\nTherefore, Comet Halley’s orbital period is\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{912\\text{ months}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. Comet Halley orbits the sun every 75 years.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "With the correction, Comet Halley’s orbital period is \\(75\\) years.\n\n\\[\n75 \\times 12 = 900\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{900\\text{ months}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Great. Now let's take that a step further. How many times would Comet Halley appear during Bill's 150-year lifetime? Additionally, Bill's lifetime lasts exactly 150 years.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Comet Halley appears once every \\(75\\) years. Over Bill’s \\(150\\)-year lifetime:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{150}{75}=2\n\\]\n\nTherefore, Comet Halley would appear **\\(\\boxed{2\\text{ times}}\\)** during Bill’s lifetime.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "I should also tell you: Bill's father saw Comet Halley when he was 32 years old.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Bill’s father seeing Comet Halley at age \\(32\\) does not change the calculation for Bill’s lifetime. Since appearances occur every \\(75\\) years:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{150}{75}=2\n\\]\n\nThus, over a \\(150\\)-year lifetime, Bill would experience\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2\\text{ appearances}}\n\\]\n\nThe father’s sighting would only help determine the exact calendar years of the appearances if Bill’s birth year or age relative to his father were also given.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Good, now using that, can you calculate: How old was Bill when he saw Comet Halley for the first time? One more thing you should know: Bill saw Comet Halley a second time when he was three times the age his father was when his father saw Comet Halley.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Bill saw Comet Halley for the second time at:\n\n\\[\n3 \\times 32 = 96\\text{ years old}\n\\]\n\nSince Comet Halley appears every \\(75\\) years, his first sighting was:\n\n\\[\n96 - 75 = 21\n\\]\n\nTherefore, Bill was \\(\\boxed{21\\text{ years old}}\\) when he saw Comet Halley for the first time.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "One more thing — Bill is alive for the entire 150-year period being considered.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Bill’s second sighting occurred when he was:\n\n\\[\n3 \\times 32 = 96\\text{ years old}\n\\]\n\nSince Comet Halley appears every \\(75\\) years, his first sighting was:\n\n\\[\n96 - 75 = 21\\text{ years old}\n\\]\n\nBecause Bill lived through the entire \\(150\\)-year period, both sightings at ages \\(21\\) and \\(96\\) occurred during his lifetime. Therefore:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{21\\text{ years old}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. Bill's father saw Comet Halley when he was 30 years old.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Bill’s second sighting occurred when he was:\n\n\\[\n3 \\times 30 = 90\\text{ years old}\n\\]\n\nSince Comet Halley appears every \\(75\\) years, his first sighting was:\n\n\\[\n90 - 75 = 15\\text{ years old}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, Bill was \\(\\boxed{15\\text{ years old}}\\) when he saw Comet Halley for the first time.",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
